ow fortunately the fda has  cracked down  on some of those companies um that have  um  false labeling um but you know with so  many companies out there now  it's really difficult to um  to you know for the fda to keep up with  all of them and track them down if  they're  if they're bad players um but since this  is not regulated by the fda  this is a self-regulated market some  companies  have higher standards and are assured  making sure that the products they are  producing  are what they say they are that they are  safe that they do  utilize third-party laboratory testing  that you know there are no residual  solvents or molds or  microbes that could actually cause  damage to patients  um making sure that those are not  present or not present at levels where  they could potentially cause harm  so um being an educated consumer is  really  vital in this market that's  that's a tremendous  set of comments and guidelines that all  parents should follow it's critically  important  to know that the company that you're  using  is actually legitimate there's some  estimates  that there are over three thousand  companies  providing hemp based products in the  united states today  if you had a crystal ball what do you  foresee in the near future  regarding medical cannabis in south  carolina  and you know i was uh privileged to  attend the la  the last medical university at south  carolina's conference that  that you uh put on  um and got to meet and spend a little  bit of time  with one of your state senators tom  davis  um give us an idea of how you see  uh you know his uh efforts in  champion legalization and  and your experience in in this space  today  well um i i pretty much threw the  crystal ball out the window last week  when we all got put on shot  shut down because of the coronavirus  [Laughter]  um if you asked me that question a week  or two ago i might have had a a  more articulate answer but um  today i i i don't know that the crystal  ball  theory is going 