  hearing on the bill today in the senate  and senate medical affairs committee  and of course um that got cancelled  uh we were all supposed to have a  hearing next week on the house version  of the bill  also canceled so it's a little hard now  to predict i'm hopeful  that they will come back into session  and  you know see the need to go ahead and  get this thing  moved because you know we are in a  health crisis  and um you know i  you know it's i have no idea whether you  know cannabinoid therapy would in any  way  help um with the coronavirus but  certainly with  people's health in general um you know  obviously we knew there are benefits  so it's very possible that they could  um do extend the session into the summer  and finish things up  or it may be a situation where we have  to start a new  um in january but you know that just  sort of remains to be seen at this point  well we do know that  is one of the important physiologic  systems that do protect us  against infection and so  just theoretically it would make sense  that  if our endocannabinoid system was in  good shape  we would be able to weather a viral  infection  much better than those that had an  endocannabinoid  deficiency syndrome  that makes sense well  how can parents patients and other  supporters get involved in your advocacy  efforts  to help bring safe access to cannabis  products for patients  like your daughter  that's another great question so like i  said we do have an organization sc  compassionate care alliance we are  a charitable organization um we're  registered with the secretary of state  and we're in the process of finally  finalizing our 501c3 paperwork for the  irs  so we um we do accept donations  and financial support goes a long way  for any non-profit as you can imagine  we're very small  but we do a tremendous amount of work  our involvement with the musc  annual medical cannabis update  conference where we bring in  speakers from all over the united states  now  that 